---
import AppShell from '../../layouts/AppShell.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../../components/Breadcrumb.astro';

export const prerender = true;

const title = 'Hire an AI Automation Specialist | Neil Busque';
const description = 'Hire Neil Busque to automate lead handling, follow-up, reporting, CRM upkeep, and repetitive operations with n8n, Zapier, GHL, and AI agents.';
const canonical = 'https://busqueneil.com/hire/ai-automation';

const service = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'ProfessionalService',
  name: 'AI Automation Consultant | Neil Busque',
  url: canonical,
  image: 'https://busqueneil.com/og.png',
  provider: { '@id': 'https://busqueneil.com/#person' },
  areaServed: ['New Jersey', 'New York', 'United States', 'Remote'],
  serviceType: ['AI automation', 'Workflow automation', 'Business process automation', 'CRM automation'],
  description,
};
---
<AppShell title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} active="hire">
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <Breadcrumb items={[
      { name: 'Home', url: 'https://busqueneil.com/' },
      { name: 'Hire', url: 'https://busqueneil.com/hire' },
      { name: 'AI Automation', url: canonical },
    ]} />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(service)} />
  </Fragment>

  <header class="page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow"><span class="idx">∗</span> Hire · AI Automation</p>
    <h1>Automate the <span class="accent">busywork</span> with AI.</h1>
    <p class="lede">I turn repeated manual work into workflows your team can see, understand, and trust. Some use AI. Many do not need it.</p>
  </header>

  <article class="article-page" style="padding-top: 8px;">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What I automate</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Leads.</strong> Capture, enrich, route, and follow up automatically, so nothing sits and goes cold.</li>
        <li><strong>Follow-up and nurture.</strong> Timely, personalized sequences across email and SMS, triggered by what people actually do.</li>
        <li><strong>Ops and admin.</strong> Data entry, reporting, CRM cleanup, and handoffs that eat your team's hours.</li>
        <li><strong>Content and research.</strong> AI agents that draft, summarize, and pull together information on a schedule.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Plain automation vs AI agents</h2>
      <p>When the steps never change, I build a normal workflow because it is cheaper and more predictable. I add an agent when the task involves messy input, a judgment call, or a draft a person should review. Here is <a href="/guides/build-ai-agent-claude-code">how those agents work</a>.</p>

      <h2>Work you can check</h2>
      <p>At an agency I shipped more than 20 production n8n workflows across over 10 client accounts, plus an onboarding system that cut a 30-day process to 7 days. See <a href="/work">the work</a> before we talk.</p>

      <h2>Let's find your time sinks</h2>
      <p>Tell me where your team loses hours. Email <a href="mailto:busqueneil@gmail.com">busqueneil@gmail.com</a> or message me on <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/neilbusque" rel="me">LinkedIn</a>. Want the engineering angle instead? See <a href="/hire/ai-engineer">hire me as an AI engineer</a>, or the full <a href="/hire">hire page</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </article>

  <div class="hire-cta v8-card">
    <p class="guarantee">I keep working until you are proud of it. If I am not the right fit, I will tell you on the first call.</p>
    <div class="hero-ctas">
      <a class="btn-sun" href="/contact">Tell me what you need</a>
      <a class="btn-ghost" href="https://wa.me/19083164140?text=Hi%20Neil%2C%20I%20want%20to%20hire%20you">Or message on WhatsApp</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</AppShell>
